# Patterns to ignore when building Helm chart packages.
# Shell glob matching, relative path matching, and negation (prefixed with !).
# One pattern per line.
#
# ⚠️ Deliberately MINIMAL. This chart had no .helmignore until #1597, so every
# pattern added here CHANGES what ships in tenant-api-<version>.tgz. The one
# entry below excludes a file that did not exist before, which keeps the
# packaged chart byte-identical to what it was — do not extend this file with
# the usual boilerplate (README.md, .git, *.swp …) without checking what that
# would remove from the published artifact.
#
# NB: Helm's .helmignore matcher does NOT support `**` (it errors and aborts
# `helm template` / `helm install`). A bare basename already matches at any
# depth. (Same constraint documented in helm/da-portal/.helmignore.)

# Container SAST L2 lint variant, NOT a deployment profile — it turns all three
# rbac scope axes to enforce so the `{{- if }}` arms get rendered and linted.
# `helm package helm/tenant-api` runs on every tenant-api release
# (.github/workflows/release.yaml) and pushes to oci://<registry>/charts, so
# without this line a values file with every axis pre-enforced would ship inside
# the chart customers pull, sitting next to values.yaml.
#
# This does NOT affect the lint variant's purpose: check_iac_helm.py renders it
# via `helm template <chart> -f <repo-path>`, reading the file from the
# repository by path rather than from the packaged chart.
values-scope-enforce.yaml
